==============================================================================
H045 -- THE NEGATIVE ENERGY DENSITY: CROSSING, REACHABILITY, VERDICT
==============================================================================
  rho_Lambda = 5.8450058e-27 kg/m^3     Lam^4 = 5.2532292e-10 J/m^3
  a_0 footings: canonical 9.3619e-11, alternative 1.1279e-10 m/s^2

==============================================================================
PART A -- WHERE DOES rho CROSS ZERO EXACTLY?
==============================================================================

  f(u) = u^2 - 2 ln(1+u) - 2/(1+u) + 1,    rho/Lam^4 = -f(u)
  f'(u) = 2u*mu_2(u) > 0 for u > 0   =>   f strictly increasing

  u*      = 1.223856281422084750007817
  K* = u*^2 = 1.497824197576293106000919
  residual f(u*) = 0.0
  rho(u*)/Lam^4  = 0.0
  [PASS] A1 [ONE CROSSING] f is strictly increasing on u > 0 (f'(u) = 2u mu_2(u)),
      f(0) = -1 and f -> +inf, so rho = -Lam^4 f crosses zero EXACTLY ONCE
         measured: df/du > 0 at all 10 sampled u in [1e-6,1e3]: True; f(1e-6)=-1.0, f(1e3)=999987.0
         threshold: df/du > 0 for every u > 0, and f changes sign
         The crossing is unique. The vacuum rho = +Lam^4 is a MAXIMUM along the
         gradient direction, not a minimum -- see Part C.

